WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.780
Fans of Hawkins, Indiana and the Upside Down
will finally get to revisit their favorite

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:09.530
characters when Stranger Things returns for
its much-anticipated third season on Netflix

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.260
in July 2019.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:17.040
Whether you're a longtime fan or a relative
newcomer, be sure to read this before you

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.620
watch.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.920
Most of the details about Stranger Things
3 are being kept under wraps, but we do know

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.100
a few things to expect from the new season.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.320
For one thing, we'll get to see the kids hanging
out together in summer for the first time,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.550
which means no more battling monsters in between
classes and instead battling monsters between

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.800
visits to the community pool and Hawkins'
brand new mall.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:41.780
We don't yet know what the new threat will
be exactly, but we also don't know if the

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.260
Mind Flayer from season 2 is completely out
of the picture yet.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.100
There are also sure to be plenty of problems
beyond the creatures from the Upside Down,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.180
in the form of the apparently corrupt Mayor
Kline, played by Cary Elwes.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.320
In terms of where the characters will be when
the new season starts, we know from the most

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.340
recent trailer that Dustin has just returned
from summer camp.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.160
Several relationships from season 2 will carry
over as well, including the father-daughter

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.010
dynamic between Sheriff Hopper and Eleven
and the romantic ties between Eleven and Mike,

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.080
and Lucas and Max.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.900
Our favorite Hawkins kids are growing up so
fast!

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.970
The first season of Stranger Things is set
in November of 1983, while the second season

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.420
picks up nearly a year later, kicking things
off in Halloween of 1984.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.440
"Trick or treat."

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.600
"You want to go trick-or-treating?!"

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.040
That kind of jump through time allows the
show to play with different pop culture references

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:40.790
and developments with each new season, but
it's also a necessity for a series that stars

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.840
rapidly aging young actors.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.990
With that in mind, season 3 will time jump
yet again by nearly a year, anchoring its

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:53.300
story in the summer of 1985, almost two full
years after the beginning of the series.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.070
The core cast of adventurous kids, telekinetic
powerhouses, and increasingly concerned adults

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:04.340
will be returning for Season 3, but the next
arc of Stranger Things is also set to introduce

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.380
several new pieces of the show's ensemble
cast.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.760
We might not know all the surprises, but here's
who to watch for.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.980
An icon of 1980s cinema will join the show
this year, as Cary Elwes, of Princess Bride

00:02:16.989 --> 00:02:22.280
fame, steps up to play Mayor Kline, an image-conscious
politician who's more concerned with advancing

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.120
his career than dealing with horrifying monsters
from an alternate dimension attacking his

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.040
constituents.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.800
Jake Busey will also join the show as a new
major player in the Hawkins community, playing

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.880
a shady, snarky reporter named Bruce

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.249
In terms of new young actors joining the series,
we have two big names to add there as well,

00:02:41.249 --> 00:02:44.860
the first being Maya Hawke, the daughter of
Ethan Hawke and Uma Thurman.

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:49.540
Hawke will play new series regular Robin,
who works with Steve at Starcourt Mall and

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.420
whose life is changed when she discovers a
dark secret.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:54.520
"How many children are you friends with?"

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:00.099
Francesca Reale, who stars in Netflix's Haters
Back Off has also joined the series in a recurring

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.060
role as Heather, a lifeguard at the local
pool.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.480
Given what's happened in swimming pools in
the series before, we have to ask: could Heather

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.719
be the new Barb?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:14.760
Perhaps the biggest mystery we've yet to learn
much about in Stranger Things 3 is exactly

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.680
who or what the Big Bad will be this time
around.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.740
Season 1 introduced us to the horrors of the
lab that created Eleven, and ultimately gave

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.580
us access to the Upside Down and its signature
monster, the Demogorgon.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.640
Season 2 gave us the Demo-dogs on its way
to revealing the terrifying power and size

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:32.780
of the Mind Flayer.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.780
As we've already discussed, that final shot
of season 2 seems to suggest the Mind Flayer

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.920
is not entirely done with Hawkins yet, but
that doesn't mean it will be back right away.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.680
In the Season 3 trailer, we get a look at
two entirely new threats that we can definitely

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.040
say look like enemies.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:53.989
In addition to a rather unpleasant-looking
man armed with a silenced pistol, wandering

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:59.060
through a hall of mirrors, there's that hideous,
asymmetrical new monster roaring in a hallway.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.620
It certainly looks like another resident of
the Upside Down has broken free to terrorize

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.020
Hawkins, but what exactly is it, and how is
it different from what we've seen before?

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.220
The kids always name their terrifying foes,
so what will they call this one?

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:16.780
All of the Stranger Things monsters so far
have taken their names from monsters found

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:21.980
in Dungeons &amp; Dragons, and this new guy sure
doesn't look like a Gelatinous Cube.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.320
"Gelatinous Cube eats village.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.140
I think it's terrific."

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:30.260
Stranger Things is a show very much steeped
in the atmosphere of what it was like to be

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.980
a kid in the 1980s, so it was bound to get
around to mall culture eventually.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.840
In season 3, that time has come at last.

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:43.120
As the show revealed in teasers last year,
1985 is the year Hawkins, Indiana finally

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.220
gets a shopping center.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:49.220
The Starcourt Mall is the newest local attraction,
drawing kids and adults alike to hang out

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.220
in the food court or visit the Waldenbooks
and Sam Goody.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.840
Steve works there, and the trailer also hints
that many Hawkins residents aren't too happy

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.220
with Mayor Kline for bringing the mall to
town in the first place.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.540
Apart from the mall, since summer's in full
bloom we'll also get a look at the Hawkins

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:09.040
community pool, where the trailer reveals
Billy is working alongside the brand-new Heather

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.040
as a lifeguard.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:15.320
Then there's the Hawkins Post, the town newspaper
where new character Bruce works and where

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.180
Nancy and Jonathan might end up for one reason
or another.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:24.040
Because Stranger Things is a famously secretive
series, any information we can get about the

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.780
new season at all is valuable, and that includes
things that arrive out of context.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.660
That's why it was so exciting for fans earlier
this year when Netflix dropped a brief teaser

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.980
which revealed all eight episode titles for
the third season.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:41.600
"The Case of the Missing Lifeguard" doesn't
bode well for Heather and Billy, and "The

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.540
Bite" certainly seems ominous, but the big
one is the season finale: "The Battle of Starcourt."

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.700
It seems like the brand new mall might not
survive the season, for reasons that have

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.640
nothing to do with declining sales.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.680
Stranger Things is a show which proudly and
earnestly wears its influences on its sleeve,

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.990
in part because of the blend of genre stories
that inspired it, and in part because it's

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:06.680
the story of a group of kids who are, at heart,
huge nerds.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.550
These kids live and breathe the pop culture
which surrounds them, which is how we get

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:15.360
the main characters dressed up like Ghostbusters,
scenes of the kids digging through the D&amp;D

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.370
Monster Manual to put names to their monstrous
enemies, and all the comic book references

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.780
that Dustin and Lucas share.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.160
"Do you think Eleven was born with powers like an X-Man or

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.660
acquired them like Green
Lantern?"

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:32.560
Since the third season is set in 1985, we
can expect certain influences to play out

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.670
in real time, including the box office success
of Back to the Future and The Goonies, an

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:40.400
adventure that's almost tame by Stranger Things
standards.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:45.200
Those are are far from the only films we should
look to as an inspiration for the new season,

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:50.780
though, as creators Matt and Ross Duffer teased
John Carpenter's The Thing as one major inspiration.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.960
Meanwhile, on the other end of the scale,
star David Harbour has mentioned that the

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:59.640
new season will also take a few cues from
the Chevy Chase private eye comedy Fletch.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.440
That's a pretty big shift in tone, but Stranger
Things has shown in the past that it can pull

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.100
off some pretty great comedy along with the
scares.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.780
Between the Demogorgon and the Mind Flayer,
we've already seen plenty of disgusting monsters

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.620
invading from the Upside Down in the past
two seasons.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.800
This time, though, we should probably expect
it to get a little more nasty.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.940
According to co-creator Ross Duffer,

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:26.400
"While it's our most fun season, it also turns
out to be our grossest season."

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.680
"I know, I know, it doesn't look like much.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.060
A little gross even.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.720
But consider this…"

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:36.480
With the creators drawing inspiration from
The Thing and its infamous monstrosity, and

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:40.441
citing the films of David Cronenberg and zombie
auteur  George Romero

00:07:40.441 --> 00:07:44.860
as major influences, we could be in for a
whole new level of body horror.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.660
And that's before we get into the scale of
things.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.360
Season 2 gave us a sprawling series of tunnels
that seemed like they were infecting the entire

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.860
city, and that's not slowing down as we move
into the next season, either.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.560
The still-mysterious new threat was even played
up by Noah Schnapp, who plays Will Byers,

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:01.360
when he said

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.020
"The threat is… it's brutal.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.140
It gets bad.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.730
It's very big... like it's taking over Hawkins."

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:11.780
The wait between seasons of Stranger Things
has been a long one, but that doesn't mean

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:15.740
the franchise has just completely shut down
in the time since we last saw the kids from

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:16.320
Hawkins.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.760
In fact, the world of Stranger Things has
only expanded in the time since the last new

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.920
episode was released.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:26.040
If you're really missing this world and its
characters, you can dig into some tie-in reading

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:26.660
right now.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.440
"I am on a curiosity voyage ...

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:30.800
And I need my paddles to travel.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:31.940
These books...

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.020
these books are my paddles."

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:40.059
In the world of prose, we now have an official
Stranger Things companion book, Worlds Turned

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.100
Upside Down, along with two tie-in novels.

00:08:43.469 --> 00:08:47.260
Suspicious Minds tells the story of Eleven's
mother and the experiments that were done

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.600
on her, and Darkness on the Edge of Town,
flashes back to a story of Sheriff Hopper's

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.860
time as a cop in New York City in the 1970s.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.340
In the comics world, there are also new stories
to dig into.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:03.760
In the fall of 2018, Dark Horse Comics launched
a four-issue Stranger Things miniseries that

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.860
tells the story of what happened to Will Byers
during the time he was stuck in the Upside

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:08.360
Down.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.960
The company has also announced Stranger Things:
Six, another new miniseries set to tell the

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.380
story of a different girl experimented on
at the Hawkins lab.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:22.440
After its debut season became a pop culture
phenomenon on Netflix, It took 15 months for

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.580
Stranger Things to return for Round 2.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:29.480
For some fans, that seemed like an eternity,
but that wait time has already been overtaken

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.200
by the long wait before the arrival of Season
3.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:36.580
"How long is a while … A year?"

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:37.460
A year?

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:41.820
By the time we get to the new episodes, we'll
have been waiting for nearly two years.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:47.900
The delay between seasons stretched on into
2018 with no real updates, until Netflix vice

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:52.899
president of original programming Cindy Holland
made it clear last summer that we'd be waiting

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.680
a little while, and that Netflix was fine
with that.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.140
Holland told a very patient audience

00:09:58.500 --> 00:09:59.960
"It's a hand-crafted show.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:04.040
The Duffer brothers and Shawn Levy work really
hard and they understand the stakes are high.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:07.720
They want to deliver something bigger and
better than what they did last year."

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.860
With everything we've seen so far, we're betting
season 3 will be worth the wait.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:17.520
Now that the third season of Stranger Things
is finally almost upon us after a very long

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:22.410
wait, it's time to once again ask the question
of how much longer the show will go on.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.440
Will we get a fourth season.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.120
A fifth?

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:25.540
Do we hope for a sixth?

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:30.259
Will we follow Lucas, Dustin, Will, Mike,
and Eleven as they go off to college and encounter

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.220
the pop culture of the early '90s?

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:36.459
This is something the Duffer brothers and
executive producer Shawn Levy have addressed

00:10:36.459 --> 00:10:40.670
before, and the answer seems to be that the
shortest run we'll get at this point is four

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:41.780
seasons of the show.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:46.660
At one point the Duffer brothers were considering
wrapping things up with Season 4 for sure,

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.520
but now they're considering an expansion.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:49.420
As Levy said,

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:53.980
"The truth is we're definitely going four
seasons and there's very much the possibility

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:54.660
of a fifth.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.600
Beyond that, it becomes I think very unlikely."

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:02.639
They might not get to the '90s, or even experience
the confusion and disappointment of seeing

00:11:02.639 --> 00:11:07.329
Ghostbusters II, but that means we still have
a while left to spend with the Hawkins gang

00:11:07.329 --> 00:11:10.040
knowing that there's at least one more adventure
to come.

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:12.700
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:16.300
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
obsessions are coming soon.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:20.180
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

